  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Forest, Agriculture, and Commodity Trade (FACT) Dialogue: Phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The FACT Dialogue aims to overcome obstacles hindering the transition to sustainable commodity production and trade, including divergent perspectives, limited market access for smallholder farmers, and fragmented governance. Supported by 28 major producer and consumer countries, the initiative focuses on Trade &amp; Markets, Support for Smallholder, Traceability and Transparency, and Research Development and Innovation. Following its launch at COP 26, senior officials agreed to prioritize actions from the roadmap, leading to the establishment of an independent FACT Secretariat tasked with facilitating actions, compiling knowledge, ensuring effective communication, and supporting logistical aspects of the dialogue.</narrative>
  </description>
